  dialogueLines:
  - subtitleText: This is a symbolic, L-shaped mass grave, designed in the mid-1960s.
      It exists only because a French survivor, Georges Bonnet, insisted that ashes
      and bone fragments were still visible here, outside the original memorial boundaries.
      His persistence forced the authorities to enclose this new burial site.
